1
00:00:00,833 --> 00:00:04,041
Part 4 weight loss interventions.

2
00:00:04,583 --> 00:00:07,375
5% loss in body weight.

3
00:00:07,583 --> 00:00:11,125
What happens if these supportive measures
are unsuccessful?

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,541
If there is a 5% drop in body weight,

5
00:00:14,625 --> 00:00:17,625
you will be switched
to a complete liquid diet.

6
00:00:17,875 --> 00:00:21,291
This means that instead
of consuming calories through solid foods,

7
00:00:21,708 --> 00:00:25,958
all calories will come from liquids
which are easier to swallow.

8
00:00:26,291 --> 00:00:28,583
You will consume
bottles filled with liquids

9
00:00:28,583 --> 00:00:32,166
that are complete
in all the nutrients and calories needed.

10
00:00:32,625 --> 00:00:35,333
Our dietitian will provide you
with these bottles

11
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:38,708
and tell you how many bottles
to consume per day.

12
00:00:39,666 --> 00:00:44,000
Although this may not sound appetizing,
the benefits of a liquid diet

13
00:00:44,291 --> 00:00:48,125
are ease of counting calories
and the ease of swallowing.

14
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,916
You will not have to put
enormous amounts of effort into chewing

15
00:00:51,916 --> 00:00:55,750
and swallowing food, while your doctor
and their team can make sure

16
00:00:55,750 --> 00:01:00,250
that you are receiving all the nutrition
and calories needed throughout treatment.

17
00:01:01,375 --> 00:01:04,375
10% loss in body weight.

18
00:01:04,375 --> 00:01:07,875
If there is a 10% or more loss of body
weight,

19
00:01:07,958 --> 00:01:10,625
a feeding tube will be inserted.

20
00:01:10,625 --> 00:01:14,416
A feeding tube
allows you to intake nourishment directly

21
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:18,166
by bypassing the need to chew and swallow
food.

22
00:01:18,291 --> 00:01:21,458
A feeding tube is an invasive intervention

23
00:01:21,666 --> 00:01:25,416
that we want to avoid due
to difficulty with insertion,

24
00:01:25,666 --> 00:01:28,625
the need to maintain it,
and a greater risk

25
00:01:28,625 --> 00:01:30,666
for irritation and infection.
